#use(std/toctree)
#use(std/table)
#use(std/pipe-table)

#section{Daily usage}::

A queue entry has two fields. The nested #tt{##row}/#tt{##cell} form takes
markup cells; the positional #tt{##row{a}{b}} form is terser — one table may
mix both:

#table(header: 1)
	#row
		#cell: Field
		#cell: Meaning
	#row{target}{Catalog name, e.g. #emph{M31}}
	#row{priority}{1 (urgent) through 5 (filler)}

For plain-text cells the pipe-table plugin trades power for source beauty:

#ptable
	Command         | Effect
	stargazer add   | Append a queue entry
	stargazer plan  | Emit tonight's schedule
	stargazer watch | Re-plan on queue changes

The scripting interfaces get a chapter of their own:

#toctree
	scripting.yamd
